{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we start by setting up the equation of the parabola and identifying its key features. Let's assume the parabola is given by \\(y = \\frac{1}{4p}x^2\\), where the vertex \\(V\\) is at the origin \\((0,0)\\) and the focus \\(F\\) is at \\((0,p)\\). The directrix of the parabola is the line \\(y = -p\\).\n\nThe segment through the focus \\(F\\) that is perpendicular to \\(\\overline{FV}\\) is a horizontal line passing through \\(F\\), which is the line \\(y = p\\). This line intersects the parabola at points \\(A\\) and \\(B\\). To find these points, we substitute \\(y = p\\) into the equation of the parabola:\n\n\\[\np = \\frac{1}{4p}x^2 \\implies x^2 = 4p^2 \\implies x = \\pm 2p.\n\\]\n\nThus, the points of intersection are \\(A = (2p, p)\\) and \\(B = (-2p, p)\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{VA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{VB}\\). The vector \\(\\overrightarrow{VA}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{VA} = (2p - 0, p - 0) = (2p, p).\n\\]\n\nThe vector \\(\\overrightarrow{VB}\\) is:\n\n","prefix_end":975,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1191,553,6243,705,279,23606,315,279,1346,370,7924,323,24588,1181,1376,4419,13,6771,594,9658,279,1346,370,7924,374,2661,553,17767,88,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,19,79,92,87,61,17,59,701,1380,279,11936,17767,53,57758,374,518,279,6238,1124,1188,15,11,15,10699,8,323,279,5244,17767,37,57758,374,518,1124,1188,15,7237,10699,568,576,2118,18356,315,279,1346,370,7924,374,279,1555,17767,88,284,481,79,59,3593,785,10238,1526,279,5244,17767,37,57758,429,374,76833,311,1124,11520,1975,1056,90,37,53,11035,8,374,264,16202,1555,12299,1526,17767,37,59,701,892,374,279,1555,17767,88,284,281,59,568,1096,1555,88184,279,1346,370,7924,518,3501,17767,32,57758,323,17767,33,59,568,2014,1477,1493,3501,11,582,27679,17767,88,284,281,57758,